\end_inset 

) we know that in an 
\begin_inset Formula $M/M/1$
\end_inset 

 that the arrivals occur as a Poisson process, and service times are exponential
ly distributed.
 This implies a birth death process with constant birth rate 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda_{k}=\lambda$
\end_inset 

 (from the Poisson process) and constant death rate (from the exponentially
 distributed service times) 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu_{k}=\mu$
\end_inset 

.
 We now give a worked example showing how the stationary distribution is
 derived using detailed balance.
 The first step is to draw the state diagram.
\layout Standard


\size tiny 

