\layout Subsection*

Answer
\layout Standard

The `death rate' 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu_{k}$
\end_inset 

 has different definitions for different parts of the state space.
 To derive the detailed balance equation we need to consider detailed balance
 for each part in turn,
\layout Subsubsection*


\begin_inset Formula $k\leq m$
\end_inset 


\layout Standard

When the system's state, 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

, is less than or equal to the number of servers we have boundary flow as
 in Figure\SpecialChar ~

\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{cap:flowAtBoundaryMMma}

\end_inset 

,
\begin_inset Float figure
wide false
collapsed false

\layout Standard
\align center 

\begin_inset Graphics
	filename ./diagrams/boundaryFlowMMinf.eps
	width 60text%

\end_inset 


\layout Caption

Flow rates at a boundary.
\begin_inset LatexCommand \label{cap:flowAtBoundaryMMma}

\end_inset 


\end_inset 

which leads to the following balance equation 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\lambda P\left(k-1\right)=k\mu P\left(k\right).\]

\end_inset 

As a result, for 
\begin_inset Formula $k=0\dots m$
\end_inset 

 we may write
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}
P\left(k\right)=\frac{\lambda}{k\mu}P\left(k-1\right).\label{eq:PkForPartA}\end{equation}

\end_inset 

It will prove convenient to define 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\rho=\frac{\lambda}{m\mu}\]

\end_inset 

which in turn gives 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\frac{\lambda}{k\mu}=\frac{m\rho}{k}\]

\end_inset 

which we substitute back into (
\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{eq:PkForPartA}

\end_inset 

) obtaining
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k\right)=\frac{m\rho}{k}P\left(k-1\right)\]

\end_inset 

and as before
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray}
P\left(k\right)=\frac{\left(m\rho\right)^{k}}{k!}P\left(0\right) & \textrm{for} & k\leq m\label{eq:probabilities}\end{eqnarray}

\end_inset 


\layout Subsubsection*


\begin_inset Formula $k>m$
\end_inset 


\layout Standard

When the system's state is greater than 
\begin_inset Formula $m$
\end_inset 

, 
\begin_inset Formula $k>m$
\end_inset 

 the flow at the boundary is as in Figure\SpecialChar ~

\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{cap:flowAtBoundaryMMmb}

\end_inset 

, the detailed balance equation is then
\begin_inset Float figure
wide false
collapsed false

\layout Standard
\align center 

\begin_inset Graphics
	filename ./diagrams/boundaryFlowMMm.eps
	width 60text%

\end_inset 


\layout Caption

Flow rates at a boundary.
\begin_inset LatexCommand \label{cap:flowAtBoundaryMMmb}

\end_inset 


\end_inset 

which leads to 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\lambda P(k-1)=m\mu P\left(k\right)\]

\end_inset 

therefore for 
\begin_inset Formula $k=m+1\dots\infty$
\end_inset 

 we may write
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k\right)=\frac{\lambda}{m\mu}P\left(k-1\right)\]

\end_inset 

using 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho=\frac{\lambda}{m\mu}$
\end_inset 

 we then have
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k\right)=\rho P\left(k-1\right)\]

\end_inset 

leading to 
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k\right)=\rho^{k-m}P\left(m\right).\]

\end_inset 

Finally we use (
\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{eq:probabilities}

\end_inset 

) and substitute 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset 

 with 
\begin_inset Formula $m$
\end_inset 

 to find 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(m\right)$
\end_inset 

 which leads to
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(m\right)=\frac{\left(m\rho\right)^{m}}{m!}P\left(0\right)\]

\end_inset 

therefore 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
P\left(k\right)=\frac{m^{m}\rho^{k}}{m!}P\left(0\right) & \textrm{for} & k>m\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

thus we can write
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(k\right)=\left\{ \begin{array}{cc}
P\left(0\right)\frac{(m\rho)^{k}}{k!}, & k\leq m\\
P\left(0\right)\frac{m^{m}\rho^{k}}{m!} & k>m\end{array}\right.\]

\end_inset 


\layout Subsection*

Normalisation Condition
\layout Standard

Once again we can compute 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(0\right)$
\end_inset 

 through normalisation
\begin_inset Formula \begin{eqnarray*}
\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}P\left(k\right) & = & 1\\
P\left(0\right)\left[\sum_{k=0}^{m-1}\frac{\left(m\rho\right)^{k}}{k!}+\sum_{k=m}^{\infty}\frac{m^{m}\rho^{k}}{m!}\right] & = & 1\\
P\left(0\right) & = & \left[\sum_{k=0}^{m-1}\frac{\left(m\rho\right)^{k}}{k!}+\sum_{k=m}^{\infty}\frac{m^{m}\rho^{k}}{m!}\right]^{-1}.\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset 

Consider the second term inside the bracket,
\begin_inset Formula \[
\sum_{k=m}^{\infty}\frac{m^{m}}{m!}\rho^{k}=\frac{m^{m}\rho^{m}}{m!}\sum_{k=m}^{\infty}\rho^{k-m}\]

\end_inset 

substitute in 
\begin_inset Formula $k^{\prime}=k-m$
\end_inset 

 and we obtain
\begin_inset Formula \[
\frac{m^{m}\rho^{m}}{m!}\sum_{k^{\prime}=0}^{\infty}\rho^{k^{\prime}}=\frac{m^{m}\rho^{m}}{m!}\frac{1}{1-\rho}\]

\end_inset 

because, as we saw in Section\SpecialChar ~

\begin_inset LatexCommand \ref{sec:MM1Stationary}

\end_inset 

 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\rho^{k}=\frac{1}{1-\rho}\]

\end_inset 

 if 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho<1$
\end_inset 

.
 Thus we have
\begin_inset Formula \[
P\left(0\right)=\left[\sum_{k=0}^{m-1}\frac{\left(m\rho\right)^{k}}{k!}+\frac{m^{m}\rho^{m}}{m!\left(1-\rho\right)}\right]^{-1}.\]

\end_inset 

Note that this relies on 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho<1$
\end_inset 

, if 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda\geq m\mu$
\end_inset 

 the system has no stationary distribution.
