 The Erlang loss system may be analysed as a birth-death process with birth
 rate 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\lambda_{k}=\left\{ \begin{array}{cc}
\lambda & k=0,1,\dots,m-1\\
0 & k\geq m\end{array}\right.\]

\end_inset 

 and death rate 
\begin_inset Formula \[
\mu_{k}=\left\{ \begin{array}{cc}
k\mu & k=0,1,\dots,m\\
0 & k>m\end{array}\right.\]

\end_inset 

 
\emph on 
Note: when 
\begin_inset Formula $k>m$
\end_inset 

, it doesn't matter what 
\begin_inset Formula $\mu_{k}$
\end_inset 

 is as we never reach this state.
